        "behaviour": [
          "Choose / Design / Connect task rail beside a persistent preview. Single click selects a list row; double-click or Enter opens Design.",
          "Nested element list follows parent/sibling order, with type icons and hover/focus help. Drag rows within a group to reorder; grouped children stay together. Depth sits under Position & size after horizontal/vertical position, with later items appearing in front.",
          "Canvas elements move on the first press and resize using eight edge/corner handles, with image proportions, keyboard controls, Escape and Undo/Redo. Automatic layout groups explain their placement limits.",
          "Dragging preview borders changes the available editor area. Game dimensions and zoom are separate; Focus preview enlarges the game view.",
          "Connect names the selected element and shows its type in smaller text. Ordered button actions, example variables and opening/closing tests explain overlay and blocking-dialog behavior.",
          "Apply/Cancel, retained drafts, shared-look confirmation, source-conflict review and protected template controls remain available in the fictional sample.",
          "Editing sections remember open/closed state per element and editing step. Form updates retain scroll and keyboard focus. Picker close returns focus to its launcher; removing a focused control returns to its section heading.",
          "This approval selects the browser design reference. Real source editing, durable saves, asset discovery and Ren'Py execution retain their product-task acceptance requirements."
        ],
        "deviations": [
          "The browser reference uses fictional in-memory data and simplified fonts, images, container reflow, scrolling, styles and components, as documented in the comparison notes. These prototype limits do not waive production behavior or acceptance."
